== Demonstration B ==
   ok   A killed worker loses ownership and the work is re-leased under a new fencing token
        attempt 1 (pid 369) is "killed"; the task is now on token g1a2
   ok   A worker presumed dead cannot overwrite the attempt that replaced it
        its lease expired without a heartbeat; it later presented token g1a1 and was rejected (task is accepted)
   ok   A new coordinator resumes from persisted state alone
        the second coordinator fenced 1 in-flight attempt(s), finished the mission, and exited 0
   ok   An orphaned worker is stopped rather than left running
        pid 592 outlived the coordinator that started it and was stopped on recovery
   ok   A duplicate delivery changes nothing, and a conflicting one is quarantined
        5 redelivered requests ignored; the repeated command returned the original mission; the conflicting one was refused: "Idempotency key demo-b-submit was reused with a different body"
   ok   Revising an upstream contract invalidates exactly what depended on it
        delivery.engine.implement: rerun_required; delivery.integrate: downstream_blocked; reliability.knowledge: rerun_required; review.packet: downstream_blocked; delivery.report.implement: rerun_required
   ok   A review decision resting on stale evidence cannot be approved by mistake
        the pending decision was superseded, its draft withdrawn, and the mission reopened
   ok   Only affected work is redone, and the result is verified again
        discovery, criteria, plan and decomposition were not rerun; engine and report were rebuilt against contract v2; all 5 criteria pass again at generation 4
   ok   State reconciles after all of it
        budget tree reconciles; event chain intact; mission review_ready with a fresh decision requested

