== Demonstration H ==
   ok   The simpler configuration is a coordination-level candidate with its own version
        coordination v1 → candidate: Sets independent_verification to false: no verification swarm is formed and the integrated result is accepted on delivery's own combined tests.
   ok   Both configurations run the same seeded missions end to end
        8 complete fixture missions per configuration from held-out set missions-A; a defect is injected into a first attempt in about half of them
   ok   The simpler configuration really is cheaper and faster
        worker invocations per mission 12.875 → 10; completion 3778 ms → 2819 ms
   ok   What it gives up is measured by an oracle, not assumed
        defects reaching an accepted result per mission 0 → 0.625; truly correct missions 1 → 0.375 (difference -0.625, 95% interval -0.875 to -0.25)
   ok   The decision follows the frozen rule
        reject: Rejected: no more defects escape failed. Acceptance criteria that fail on results the mission accepted: candidate 5, incumbent 0, across 8 episodes.
   ok   A second simplification is put to the same gate: no interface agreement before parallel work
        Removes the interface-agreement step: no contract task, and delivery workstreams take the acceptance criteria as input instead of a pinned contract. Run on missions-B; the workstreams disagreed about the shared record in 5 of 8 episodes (an assumed rate).
   ok   The cost of the step and the cost of going without it are both measured
        the agreement step costs 1 worker invocations and 383 ms per mission; a mission where the workstreams disagreed cost 1 more invocations and 774 ms more than the same mission with the agreement
   ok   Integration failures and quality are reported, not assumed
        integration failures per mission 0 → 0.625; truly correct missions 1 → 1; invocations 11.75 → 12 (difference 0.25, 95% interval -0.5 to 0.75); completion 3358 ms → 3698 ms
   ok   The decision follows the frozen rule, whatever it is
        inconclusive: No demonstrated improvement: truly_correct_missions is no worse (95% interval 0 to 0, margin 0), but cost did not fall (worker_invocations_per_mission changed by 0.25), so the simplification saves nothing.

